00:10:14.847 --> 00:10:16.896
you throw the power behind it right in the way you stand

257
00:10:16.896 --> 00:10:19.462
and just because of my speed and my skill,

258
00:10:19.462 --> 00:10:22.535
that's why I excelled so fast in the sport.

259
00:10:22.535 --> 00:10:26.285
So it had to be quite an experience to know

260
00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:33.669
that you were the best in the world at such a young age.

261
00:10:33.669 --> 00:10:36.262
I mean, it's not something you think about

262
00:10:36.262 --> 00:10:37.997
because I'll be honest with you like-

263
00:10:37.997 --> 00:10:40.553
You're very oh shacks about all of it, you know?

264
00:10:40.553 --> 00:10:43.866
Well, my coach will tell you something like you know...

265
00:10:43.866 --> 00:10:45.719
I mean, I was very good at what I did,

266
00:10:45.719 --> 00:10:49.276
but I never, ever got complimented by my coach.

267
00:10:49.276 --> 00:10:51.382
He never said, oh, this is what you're good at.

268
00:10:51.382 --> 00:10:53.663
He only focus on the things that I was bad at.

269
00:10:53.663 --> 00:10:56.227
Even when I won the world championship, he said,

270
00:10:56.227 --> 00:10:58.386
he whispered in my ear, "You could have done better."

271
00:10:58.386 --> 00:10:59.219
You know what I mean?

272
00:10:59.219 --> 00:11:02.343
So, there's always one up on you, right?

273
00:11:02.343 --> 00:11:05.027
So, you always gotta stay grounded no matter where you are

274
00:11:05.027 --> 00:11:07.952
because when you are at the top of your game,

275
00:11:07.952 --> 00:11:09.935
all it means you have to work twice as hard to stay there.

276
00:11:09.935 --> 00:11:10.768
Yeah.

277
00:11:10.768 --> 00:11:14.114
And what did you learn about discipline and perseverance

278
00:11:14.114 --> 00:11:19.112
and meeting obstacles as a young person who is so devoted

279
00:11:19.112 --> 00:11:22.362
to this specific sport discipline?

280
00:11:22.362 --> 00:11:23.769 line:15%
I mean, like I said earlier, I mean it was...

281
00:11:23.769 --> 00:11:26.403 line:15%
It taught me what it takes to be the best in this lasering

282
00:11:26.403 --> 00:11:29.519 line:15%
and it's 110% and it's a lot of sacrifice, right?

283
00:11:29.519 --> 00:11:31.036 line:15%
Like you tell a 13 year old kid

284
00:11:31.036 --> 00:11:32.612 line:15%
to give up all the fun things,

285
00:11:32.612 --> 00:11:34.497
most would probably say no, right?

286
00:11:34.497 --> 00:11:36.037
But I knew those sacrifices would,

287
00:11:36.037 --> 00:11:37.779
it would pay off at the end.

288
00:11:37.779 --> 00:11:39.483
Good times and friends are always gonna be around

289
00:11:39.483 --> 00:11:42.089
but I think especially unique opportunities won't.

290
00:11:42.089 --> 00:11:42.931
Yeah.

291
00:11:42.931 --> 00:11:47.813
You seem to have a predisposition, like a deep understanding

292
00:11:47.813 --> 00:11:51.561
that delayed gratification is the path, right?

293
00:11:51.561 --> 00:11:54.487
Like you're able as a young person going through adolescence

294
00:11:54.487 --> 00:11:56.721
and the teen years where there's a lot of temptation

295
00:11:56.721 --> 00:11:59.751
to kinda do a lot of different things and get in trouble

296
00:11:59.751 --> 00:12:03.607
to just be very focused on the larger goal.

297
00:12:03.607 --> 00:12:06.095
Well, I mean, I knew I had to work harder

298
00:12:06.095 --> 00:12:06.928
at a lot of things.

299
00:12:06.928 --> 00:12:08.520
'Cause even in school, let's go back to school,

300
00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:10.410
I mean, I had a learning disability.

301
00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.208
You know I was put in a special class.

302
00:12:12.208 --> 00:12:14.506
And I knew I had to work twice as hard as everybody else

303
00:12:14.506 --> 00:12:17.468
but I was determined to graduate with honors and I did.

304
00:12:17.468 --> 00:12:19.852
But I knew for someone like me I had to work twice as hard

305
00:12:19.852 --> 00:12:22.408
even when I was a child, my left leg was growing

306
00:12:22.408 --> 00:12:24.550
at a faster rate than my right leg, it's longer,

307
00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:26.421
it's stronger, the foot is bigger.

308
00:12:26.421 --> 00:12:27.646
And doctors told my parents

309
00:12:27.646 --> 00:12:29.989
that I'd never excel in athleticism.

310
00:12:29.989 --> 00:12:33.173
So when you're left with that, you know you got challenges,

311
00:12:33.173 --> 00:12:34.302
but are you gonna hang on to that

312
00:12:34.302 --> 00:12:35.875
or are you gonna prove to people what you can do

313
00:12:35.875 --> 00:12:37.220
with what you don't have?

314
00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:38.826
Right, you're the kind of person who

315
00:12:38.826 --> 00:12:41.146
when somebody tells you, you can't do it,

316
00:12:41.146 --> 00:12:43.108
that's just fuel for the fire, right?

317
00:12:43.108 --> 00:12:43.941
Exactly.

318
00:12:43.941 --> 00:12:45.132
(both laughs)

319
00:12:45.132 --> 00:12:49.424
But here's the thing, you become world champion at 17

320
00:12:49.424 --> 00:12:52.639
and I'm just baffled at why you didn't stick with it

321
00:12:52.639 --> 00:12:54.665
