322
00:12:54.665 --> 00:12:56.978
Because that was never my dream.

323
00:12:56.978 --> 00:12:58.145
Like my dream-

324
00:12:59.704 --> 00:13:02.444
It was your dream enough to be so disciplined

325
00:13:02.444 --> 00:13:04.732
and focused and train so hard for it.

326
00:13:04.732 --> 00:13:05.787
Well, that was...

327
00:13:05.787 --> 00:13:09.372
Like boosting was a problem to a solution, right?

328
00:13:09.372 --> 00:13:11.391
Or a solution to a problem I should say, right?

329
00:13:11.391 --> 00:13:13.465
What I wanted to do from as young as I could remember,

330
00:13:13.465 --> 00:13:15.047
from when I was seven years old

331
00:13:15.047 --> 00:13:17.379
is I wanted to be James Bond.

332
00:13:17.379 --> 00:13:20.052
And I knew when I graduated from high school

333
00:13:20.052 --> 00:13:22.158
that I was gonna go back to Israel and I was gonna go

334
00:13:22.158 --> 00:13:24.467
into the IDF, the Israel Defense Force.

335
00:13:24.467 --> 00:13:27.049
And I was gonna really start my career at that point.

336
00:13:27.049 --> 00:13:29.267
Where did that idea come from?

337
00:13:29.267 --> 00:13:31.478
Like what's the Genesis of that dream?

338
00:13:31.478 --> 00:13:35.184
Okay, well, my family as you know they're all from Israel

339
00:13:35.184 --> 00:13:37.658
and going back every year as a child,

340
00:13:37.658 --> 00:13:39.983
I knew that members of my family were involved

341
00:13:39.983 --> 00:13:42.111
in some kind of work that were secretive

342
00:13:42.111 --> 00:13:43.250
'cause there's members of my family

343
00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:45.797
that I would only see maybe for an hour

344
00:13:45.797 --> 00:13:48.247
once every five years or whatever.

345
00:13:48.247 --> 00:13:50.304
So I knew there was something secretive there

346
00:13:50.304 --> 00:13:52.193
that just intrigued me and it just felt...

347
00:13:52.193 --> 00:13:55.287
And as I got older, I knew it was something in security.

348
00:13:55.287 --> 00:13:57.226
And it's just something that I felt that I needed to do

349
00:13:57.226 --> 00:13:59.373
that I was born to do, that I was meant to do.

350
00:13:59.373 --> 00:14:01.608
And it was on my radar from,

351
00:14:01.608 --> 00:14:03.489
like I said from as young as I could remember.

352
00:14:03.489 --> 00:14:05.624
So you had extended family members

353
00:14:05.624 --> 00:14:08.392
that were like Mossad agents or-

354
00:14:08.392 --> 00:14:10.265
I'm not gonna say Mossad, they're in security,

355
00:14:10.265 --> 00:14:11.672
won't say what.

356
00:14:11.672 --> 00:14:13.974
Security, quote, unquote, right?

357
00:14:13.974 --> 00:14:17.592
Like we can't talk about it but that's pretty romantic

358
00:14:17.592 --> 00:14:20.215
and intriguing for a young person to hear like, wow,

359
00:14:20.215 --> 00:14:21.396
what are they really doing?

360
00:14:21.396 --> 00:14:22.734
Well yeah, it just fascinated me.

361
00:14:22.734 --> 00:14:23.567
Yeah.

362
00:14:23.567 --> 00:14:26.172
Like you know, my parents speak many different languages

363
00:14:26.172 --> 00:14:30.020
so when my uncle, when he would come in and my mother

364
00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:32.432
for example she was very close to her brothers

365
00:14:32.432 --> 00:14:35.253
and she didn't want my sister and I to understand,

366
00:14:35.253 --> 00:14:38.218
they would swap languages into Russian, you know?

367
00:14:38.218 --> 00:14:40.074
And so I started to try and pick up as much Russian

368
00:14:40.074 --> 00:14:41.908
as I could to understand the conversations

369
00:14:41.908 --> 00:14:42.987
that were going on.

370
00:14:42.987 --> 00:14:45.740
So, it's kinda how we were brought up too.

371
00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:48.389
I mean, my parents never wanted us to say anything

372
00:14:48.389 --> 00:14:50.260
on the phone or you don't, you won't...

373
00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:51.507
Be careful who you make friends with,

374
00:14:51.507 --> 00:14:53.433
be careful what you tell your friends.

375
00:14:53.433 --> 00:14:55.354
So we had had that upbringing of everything

376
00:14:55.354 --> 00:14:58.189
is kind of a secret and keep it in the family sort of thing.

377
00:14:58.189 --> 00:15:00.106
Wow, so your parents,

378
00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:05.029
they were associated with security in some way?

379
00:15:05.029 --> 00:15:06.161
If they were they're really good at it

380
00:15:06.161 --> 00:15:07.043
'cause I don't know.

381
00:15:07.043 --> 00:15:08.027
You don't know.

382
00:15:08.027 --> 00:15:10.205
What did they do to make a living?

383
00:15:10.205 --> 00:15:12.789
Well, my father, he owned industries

384
00:15:12.789 --> 00:15:16.138
like he was a machinist so he bought into companies

385
00:15:16.138 --> 00:15:20.076
as he got more successful, my mom was a registered nurse.

386
00:15:20.076 --> 00:15:21.313
By day.
By day.

387
00:15:21.313 --> 00:15:22.863
But who knows that she did at night.

388
00:15:22.863 --> 00:15:23.902
(both laughs)

389
00:15:23.902 --> 00:15:25.305
Oh my God.

390
00:15:25.305 --> 00:15:28.105
But you have this idea, like this is the path for me.

391
00:15:28.105 --> 00:15:28.977
I'm gonna go to Israel

392
00:15:28.977 --> 00:15:30.166
Oh absolutely.

393
00:15:30.166 --> 00:15:31.628
And enlist in the IDF.

